    "final_text": "I fixed the bug: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`, and the full test suite passes (9 of 9).\n\n**Cause:** In `src/url-builder.js`, the code that turns the query object into a query string skipped any \"falsy\" value. It used `if (!value) continue;` in `serializeQuery` and `if (!item) continue;` for array items in `appendQueryValue`. `0` and `false` count as falsy in JavaScript, so they were dropped along with values that really were missing. Running the issue's example gave `...?dry_run=true`, exactly as reported. Array values had the same problem: `attempt: [0, 1]` came out as just `attempt=1`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/url-builder.js:126`, `:137\u2013142`): both checks now use a small helper, `isEmptyQueryValue`, which skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`. The issue's example now gives `...?dry_run=true&include_archived=false&retry=0`. The `buildUrl` API is unchanged.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/url-builder.test.js`):\n- `buildUrl keeps numeric zero and boolean false query values (ISSUE-214)` checks the exact reported case and the full expected URL.\n- `serializeQuery keeps falsy array items but still omits missing values` checks that `0` and `false` inside arrays are kept, and that `undefined`, `null` and `''` are still left out.\n\nI ran the suite with the fix temporarily removed: both new tests failed and the original 7 passed. With the fix, all 9 pass.\n\n`ISSUE.md` now ends with a `Resolution` section naming the code path (`buildUrl` \u2192 `serializeQuery` \u2192 `appendQueryValue`), the fix and both tests.\n\nDecision for you: I kept empty strings (`q: ''`) being left out of the URL, as they were before. The issue only covers `0` and `false`, and changing `''` could break callers who rely on it being dropped. If you'd rather send `q=`, remove `|| value === ''` from the helper and update the second test. One small side effect of the fix: `NaN` is now sent as `NaN` instead of being dropped.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
